sysjam themes — sources and licensing
=====================================

assets/themes/themes.txt is generated by tools/extract_themes.py from the corpus
bundled with music21 10.5.0 (https://github.com/cuthbertLab/music21). It contains
only short melodic incipits (2–8 bars) reduced to facts: scale degrees relative to
a tonic, durations, mode, meter, and a citation. No corpus file, encoding text,
layout, fingering, lyric or editorial annotation is copied.

Rule used: a source is included only if (a) the composition itself is in the
public domain (composer died before 1900 / published before 1929, or traditional),
and (b) the corpus files for it carry no restrictive notice (no "non-commercial",
"all rights reserved", or share-alike licence that would not be GPL-3.0
compatible). The resulting table is distributed with sysjam under
GPL-3.0-or-later; as public-domain melodic data it places no extra conditions on it.

Included (371 themes)
---------------------
Source (corpus dir)          Themes  Composition            Corpus file notes
---------------------------  ------  ---------------------  ---------------------------------------------
Bach chorales (bach/)          120   J.S. Bach (d. 1750);   no rights element; credit line "PDF © 2004
                                     hymn tunes, PD         Margaret Greentree, used by permission" refers
                                                            to her engraved PDF edition (jsbchorales.net);
                                                            only the soprano melody's pitches/rhythm used.
                                                            Titles/BWV via music21's chorale lists.
Beethoven quartets              15   L. van Beethoven       no rights element (Finale exports)
  (beethoven/: Op. 18, 59,           (d. 1827), PD
  74, 132, 133)
