                                                            licence restriction

(Counts per source are also written as comments at the top of themes.txt.)
Thanks to all the transcribers above and to the music21 project.

Excluded, and why
-----------------
essenFolksong/   license.txt: legal status unclear; permission only for
                 NON-COMMERCIAL distribution and use within music21 → not GPL-compatible.
ciconia/, luca/  <rights> CC-BY-SA 3.0 (M.S. Cuthbert) — editorial transcriptions of
                 mensural notation; CC-BY-SA 3.0 is not GPL-3.0 compatible.
trecento/        editorial transcriptions with no stated licence → not used.
palestrina/      "Copyright 2000, John Miller" → not used.
monteverdi/      Ut Orpheus Edizioni copyright → not used.
beach/           engraving under CC-BY-SA → not used.
schubert/        bare "Copyright ©" notice → not used.
schumann_clara/  "©" notice → not used.
leadSheet/       contains an "All Rights Reserved" file → whole directory not used.
joplin/          Maple Leaf Rag (PD, 1899) but the file points to a musescore.com user
                 upload whose licence cannot be verified → not used.
weber/           eligible ("Released to Public Domain in 1998") and read by the
                 extractor, but its opening yields no usable melodic incipit → 0 themes.
everything else  not needed (corelli CC-BY, josquin GPL-2+, cpebach MakeMusic notes,
                 miscFolk, etc. were not included to keep the provenance simple).

Every quote sysjam plays is cited in the terminal (thinking line, the TUI's
"now quoting" line and history, and the --no-tui log) as
  Title (Composer or trad., catalogue) · collection · music21 corpus · public domain
